 ### Generic Rule Marching Cubes
-**Definition:** A variant of Marching Cubes that uses a single generic rule to triangulate all 15 standard cube configurations and additional cases, eliminating the need for a lookup table [S1].
-**Pitfall:** Resolves the Type A ‘hole problem’ which occurs when at least one cube face has an intersection point in each of its four edges [S1].
-**Number:** Tested on full resolution CT and MRI of human heads on SGI Indigo 2 with 128 MB RAM [S1].
-**Comparison:** Differs from standard Marching Cubes by not requiring definition of different cube configurations, rotations, or comparisons with predefined configurations, reducing execution time [S1].
